 corporate and government reimbursement policies."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is full insurance mandatory for Bike Transportation In Burla, and what does it cover?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Full insurance is optional but highly recommended. Our IRDAI‑approved policy covers 100 % of the declared bike value against accidental damage, theft, fire, and natural calamities during transit. The policy also includes liability for any third‑party claims arising from the shipment, giving you complete peace of mind."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How are hydraulic ramp trailers loaded and unloaded safely in Burla?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The hydraulic ramp lowers at a controlled speed, aligning perfectly with the loading dock. Technicians position the bike on a padded platform, secure it with wheel chocks, and fasten high‑tensile lashings. During unloading, the ramp lifts gently, and the bike is rolled onto a pre‑prepared cradle, ensuring zero impact."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What factors influence the cost of bike parcel service in Burla?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Pricing depends on distance (approximately 850 km to major hubs), bike dimensions, selected vehicle class (standard vs. premium trailer), insurance coverage level, and any special handling requirements for cruiser or custom bikes. Transparent cost breakdowns are provided in our quote, reflecting each component clearly."}}]}
